[[File:E 022.png|thumb|[[Mooth|Mooth]], the first example of a Floating enemy]]
'''Floating Enemies''' (浮いてる敵, ''Uiteru Teki'') generally refer to enemies that have the ability to float. Pure Floating enemies' bodies are generally white or gray, but many others are hybrids and come with additional traits. Unlike [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] and [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin]], Floating is considered a trait, meaning it never overlaps with [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and can be affected by [[Special Abilities|abilities]] that target "all traits" or "Traited enemies", such as [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Shining Amaterasu]]'s [[Massive Damage]] and [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]]'s [[Strong Against]].

Note that some enemies visually levitate despite not being actually Floating. All [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal Enemies]], [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] (except [[Bears Be Back]]), [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], [[:Category:Witch Enemies|Witches]] and [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|EVA Angels]] lack Floating, along with several levitating enemies of other traits like [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]] and [[Sage of Logic Newtone]].

See [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Floating abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Slow Beam Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Floating enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Floating enemies are associated with Green [[Catfruit]], which can be obtained from the [[Growing Catfruit]] stage [[Green Envy]].
*Anti-Floating abilities are improved by the [[Sky Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]].
*Floating [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Floating|Sky Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Floating|Sky Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Floating|Sky Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Cheerful Dawn]], [[Cheerful Apex]], [[Cheerful Refuge]]
**[[Mega Menace]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Mega Menace/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Mega Menace/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Mega Menace/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*The first Floating enemy encountered in-game is [[Mooth]], but the first Floating enemy in terms of ID is [[The Face]], who has a lower ID than Mooth despite appearing later.
*[[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]] and [[Commander Bun Bun]] are the only non-[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], non-collab Floating enemies to have the Floating trait's associated color, green.
*Floating was the only trait from [[The Battle Cats]] to also appear in [[Kyoutou Project]], though one could argue the Steel type was just [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] under a different name.
**In Kyoutou Project, Floating was associated with light blue instead of green.
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], Floating was named Hikō-kei (飛行系, "Flying Group", "Flying Family", "Flying Style" or "Flying Type") and was not considered a trait, but rather one of many [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%AD%A5%E3%A5%E9%A5%AF%A5%BF%A1%BC%A4%CE%A5%BF%A5%A4%A5%D7#content_1 special non-trait types] assigned to both allied and enemy units, which were relevant for stage restrictions and unique abilities set to either buff or counter units of these types without being disabled by Seal (the game's equivalent of the Curse effect). The [[wikipedia:Ojamajo Doremi|Ojamajo Doremi]] collab unit [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A4%AA%A5%B8%A5%E3%CB%E2%BD%F7%A4%AA%A4%F3%A4%D7 Ojamajo Onpu] had a Target Type Killer ability that did up to 400% damage to Flying enemies, which was separate from the Massive Damage ability, and the [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%B6%A5%F3%A5%D3%A5%A2 allied version] of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Zambia|Zambia]] could gain the ability to boost all Flying allies' health by 20%.
*[[Owlbrow]] and his variants are the only Floating enemies to walk most of the time, with his description even poking fun at this.
**The reverse could also be applied to the Japanese descriptions of [[Super Cosmic Cyclone]] and [[Mesocosmocyclone]], which specify that they are too low to the ground to be actually floating.
*From [[Version 12.5 Update|Version 12.5]] to [[Version 13.2 Update|Version 13.2]], [[Ursamajor]]'s traits were incorrectly listed as "[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/Floating" in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]'s [[Enemy Guide]], even though he isn't a Floating enemy. This was fixed with the Enemy Guide rework in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].

